# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# routing.env — switches for the Routing Optimiser, loaded by run.command at startup.
#
# One per line, NAME=value. `#` starts a comment. Delete a line (or comment it out) to go back
# to the default. run.command echoes what it loaded, so the terminal always says which
# configuration a run used.
#
# EVERY optimisation in the engine ships behind one of these, so anything can be reverted without
# a code change. TWO of them change the answer as of 2026-08-19cn, and both are flagged below:
#   ROUTING_PROJ_FLOAT32=1   the float32 band projector (drift accepted 2026-08-24)
#   ROUTING_SEED_ZEROS=1     the seed's exact zeros survive into the genome (armed 2026-08-26)
# And as of 2026-08-27 a THIRD is under suspicion rather than established either way:
#   ROUTING_FEAS_PAR        concurrent feasibility starts. Claimed identical-by-construction; the
#                           test behind that claim used a deterministic stub and did not cover the
#                           live numba projector. Armed to 0 for one run to find out. See its block.
# This header said "Only ONE of them changes the answer" until the second one was armed. A count
# in a comment is a fact that goes stale the moment the file is edited, so it is checked here
# whenever a switch moves in or out of the answer-affecting set.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── ANSWER-AFFECTING #1 OF 2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# float32 band projector. Measured 1.598x on the projector on 2026-08-24 (15 of 15 paired rounds,
# p=0.000, against a +-2.0% floor), and the projector is ~34% of a generation, so ~20% of the
# search. It is ON here because a drift on `txn` was accepted on 2026-08-24 — but READ THE SIZE IN
# THE LOG, do not assume the size it was accepted at. The "~2 transactions" quoted at the time was
# [kernel-ab] row F's, which times a FLAT float32 kernel on a COPY of prop_raw. The SHIPPED path is
# the cell-blocked kernel on the live scaffold. The "7x" gap first reported was itself a bad
# comparison — row F at P=35 against the shipped path at P=1 — and once 19cf measured the shipped
# path at the LIVE width the two came out 1.53x apart (2.413 vs 1.577 txn on 2026-08-25 19:14).
# Since 19cf the log prints the shipped path's own figure at the live width, as both the worst
# SINGLE band and the TOTAL across all bands: a drift of 12 concentrated in one MID and a drift of
# 12 spread over fifteen are different facts. Since 19cg [kernel-ab] computes the ratio between the
# two and REFUSES to quote one when they were measured at different widths. Look for
# [proj-config], and quote the SHIPPED figures.
#
# TWO THINGS TO EXPECT IN THE LOG, both normal under this setting:
#   1. a *** FLOAT32 PROJECTOR IS ON banner, with the drift MEASURED on that run's own scaffold;
#   2. RECONCILIATION ERROR will no longer read 0. It is  sum|delivered - GA-fitness|, and
#      GA-fitness now comes from a float32 kernel while delivery stays float64, so it reads about
#      the drift. That is the setting, not a regression — but that number also stops being able
#      to detect a REAL reconciliation bug at that size. Set this to 0 to get the detector back.
# The search is chaotic, so a float32 run's trajectory differs from a float64 run's; compare end
# results, not candidate for candidate.
#
# HOW TO CONFIRM IT ACTUALLY ENGAGED (learned the expensive way on 2026-08-24). Setting the switch
# is not the same as the setting taking effect. On that run it WAS set, and a bug in the self-check
# above the banner raised, which disabled the whole cell-blocked path and took float32 down with it
# — silently, because the banner is printed after the line that raised. 5 h 22 m at the flat
# kernel's speed. Fixed in 19cd, and the failure line now says outright what it costs. So:
#   * search the log for FLOAT32 PROJECTOR IS ON. Present = it engaged. ABSENT = it did NOT,
#     whatever this file says.
#   * search for "could not run" and "FAILED to run". Either means the projector fell back to the
#     flat kernel and every timing below it is roughly half the engine's real speed.
# SET TO 0 ON 2026-08-27, restoring 19ct after the reset experiment.
# TWO reasons, neither of them "float32 broke reconciliation" — that is now DISPROVEN:
#   1. The 23:32 run (19cd, 114 gateways, FLOAT64) read RECONCILIATION ERROR 1,291. Same code
#      that read 0 on 25 Aug with 34 gateways. So the gateway set is the cause and float32 is
#      not, on a float64 run that proves it.
#   2. With this at 0 the NEXT run is a clean CODE-ONLY comparison against that 1,291: same data,
#      same projector, 19ct instead of 19cd. With it at 1 the two runs differ in two ways again,
#      which is the mistake this file has now recorded twice.
# It also keeps the detector: at 1 the error reads about the projector drift and stops being able
# to see a real reconciliation bug at that size. Set it back to 1 once the comparison is banked.
ROUTING_PROJ_FLOAT32=0

# ── MEASUREMENT (read-only blocks; none of these touch the split) ─────────────────────────────
# Paired rounds for [stage-ab]. 11 by default since 19cc: at 7 the only sign-test scores that
# clear p<=0.10 are 7/7 and 0/7, so one unlucky round buries a real effect — which is what
# happened to the lanes row at +5.0%, 6/7. Raise further if a row still reads NOT MEASURABLE.
# ROUTING_STAGE_AB_REPS=11

# [elig-cost] (19ci) splits the ELIGIBILITY stage — the largest single stage in the search — into
# REDUCE (the np.add.reduceat calls, which cannot be bit-identically re-implemented, so a floor),
# ELEMENTWISE (the fused passes, the only part any fusion can touch) and ALLOC. It costs a few
# serial passes over the population. Set to 0 to skip it; ROUTING_ELIG_COST_REPS sets the rounds.
# ROUTING_ELIG_COST=0
# ROUTING_ELIG_COST_REPS=7

# [elig-par] (19cl) sweeps the SHIPPED eligibility transform across 1/2/4/8/all-cores worker
# counts and prints the scaling curve with per-worker efficiency. ~4 s. It exists because the line
# it replaced ASSERTED that threading made this stage "several times smaller" and the 2026-08-26
# 19:24 run printed 276.9 ms serial and 258.2 ms threaded on the same page — 1.07x. READ IT LIKE
# THIS: a FLAT curve on a live-shape array means the stage is MEMORY-BANDWIDTH bound, so only fewer
# BYTES help (narrower dtype, genuinely fewer passes) and neither more threads nor more fusion can;
# a RISING curve past the shipped worker count means the 19bo half-cores default is running the
# search's largest stage at half width. Those point opposite ways, which is why it is measured.
# ROUTING_ELIG_PAR=0
#
# [width-probe] (19cm) rides in the same block: ONE full-width elementwise pass at the live shape in
# float64 and float32 — same operation, half the bytes — reported as effective GB/s. It answers the
# question [elig-par] raises but cannot: IF the stage is bandwidth-bound, how much would a narrower
# dtype buy HERE? Quoting the projector's float32 1.598x at this stage would be the same error one
# stage along. It is a CEILING on the ELEMENTWISE part only — reduceat does not halve with the
# dtype, and `apply_elig_pop` coerces to float64 on entry, so a narrower stage is a real change and
# not a flag. And it would CHANGE THE ANSWER, exactly as ROUTING_PROJ_FLOAT32 does.

# [kernel-ab] and [stage-ab] are now OFF. Every [kernel-ab] variant has a standing verdict (C, D, E
# dead; F real but answer-moving; G and chunking adopted) and [stage-ab]'s S and X rows were retired
# to standing verdicts too, so neither block can currently change a decision. Measured on the
# 2026-08-25 20:35 run: [kernel-ab] 150 s, [stage-ab] 34 s — ~184 s of a 1029.9 s run.
#
# READ WHAT THIS BUYS CORRECTLY. It is WALL CLOCK, not throughput. The search itself was 285.9 s of
# that run (28%); these two blocks run AFTER it and touch neither the split nor splits/s. A run that
# comes back 184 s sooner with the GA doing exactly the same work per second is not a faster engine,
# and the run log will not distinguish the two — this comment is the distinction.
#
# TURN THEM BACK ON (delete the line, or set to 1) THE MOMENT A NEW IDEA NEEDS DECIDING. That is the
# whole purpose of the blocks, and an idea argued from memory instead of from a paired measurement
# is how the "understated by about 7x" claim got into a log and stayed there for three builds.
ROUTING_KERNEL_AB=0
ROUTING_STAGE_AB=0

# [seed-diag] (19ck) — the eight READ-ONLY report blocks that follow the seed chain:
# held-vs-movable, reachable minimum, VAMP-positive sibling, incidence self-check, seed gradient,
# vpsum, usable-recipient, co-location and the seed unmet-band summary. ~15.8 s on the 20:35 run,
# and they change no share. They are the evidence for "is this band genuinely unreachable?", so
# leave them ON while any seed or feasibility question is open. With them off the log prints ONE
# line saying so — a skipped diagnostic must never read like a failed one.
# ROUTING_SEED_DIAG=0

# ── THE MUTED RECONCILIATION FAMILIES (19co) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ROUTING_RECON_RELEASE=0 stops the RUN-LEVEL release; ROUTING_RECON_BAR sets its threshold
# (default 1).
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. The log's muting gate is LINE-BY-LINE: a family is held unless one of ITS OWN
# lines carries a warning marker. On 2026-08-26 20:28 that held [terms], [vterms], [rung2],
# [conservation], [denom], [baseline-split], [step1] and [step2] — every family whose subject is
# the scored-vs-delivered chain — on a run that printed RECONCILIATION ERROR = 1,393 with [rung]
# attributing 100% of it to PROJECTION MATH. Each was quiet because each of its own checks passed
# on its own terms; the gate could not hear a number computed a thousand lines later.
#
# So RECONCILIATION ERROR above the bar now releases those families IN FULL, naming the number that
# opened them. The line-by-line rule is unchanged. ROUTING_LOG_ALL=1 still shows everything.

# ── THE SEED'S EXACT ZEROS (19cm) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ROUTING_SEED_ZEROS=1 — encode the seed's exactly-zero shares as -inf logits, so the GA's decode
# can reproduce them. DEFAULT 0, and 0 is the pre-19cm behaviour exactly.
#
# WHAT IT REPAIRS. The genome is logits, so the seed enters as softmax(log(clip(share, 1e-6))) and
# every exact zero comes back positive. Where the resurrected row is the ONLY VAMP-positive gateway
# in its cell, vshare self-normalises to 1 and the cell's whole VAMP returns. On 2026-08-26 that
# cost the seed 0.6419 -> 0.6461 BEFORE a single generation ran; the search gained 0.0046 over 288 s
# and 11,840 splits, and [never-worse] then shipped the SEED anyway (delivered 88 vs 89).
#
# WHY NOT JUST A SMALLER CLIP. Because vshare is SCALE-INVARIANT: s/s = 1 for any s > 0, so 1e-30 is
# exactly as bad as 1e-6. Only a true zero changes anything.
#
# WHY -inf AND NOT A MASK. A mask would have to be threaded through BOTH softmax implementations —
# numpy's and the numba fused kernel's — and any divergence between those two is a scored-vs-
# delivered bug. Both are the standard max-subtract stable softmax, so exp(-inf - m) = 0 exactly in
# both with no kernel change: the zero lives in the DATA, so the two paths cannot disagree about it.
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES. -inf + noise is -inf, so a seed's zeros are INHERITED by its descendants. That is
# the point, and it is also a behaviour change. `_init_pop`'s unanchored exploration children carry
# no -inf, so the search space is not permanently narrowed. Read [decode-loss] — it prints the
# handicap every run, switch on or off, so the fix can be priced against what the search then gains.
#
# REFUSED alongside the compressibility regulariser (it runs k-means over the logit genome, which
# -inf would turn into nan centroids). The log says so rather than silently mixing them.
#
# ── ANSWER-AFFECTING #2 OF 2 · ARMED 2026-08-26 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# ARMED because [decode-loss] priced it on the 2026-08-26 20:28 run and the number was far larger
# than the estimate it replaced: the seed's exact breach 0.341755 -> 0.640861 decoded, a handicap
# of +0.299105 paid BEFORE generation 1, against which the whole 320-generation search then
# recovered 0.0005. 35,943 rows came back from zero at exactly the 1e-6 clip floor.
#
# WHAT TO CHECK ON THE FIRST ARMED RUN, in this order:
#   1. [decode-loss] should read ~0 where it read +0.299105. Anything else is a defect in the fix,
#      and the block says so itself.
#   2. [never-worse] then answers the question this was built for: can the GA beat a seed it can
#      actually start from? It shipped the SEED on 2026-08-26 19:24 and the GA OUTPUT on 20:28,
#      both times on a delivered breach that disagrees with GA-fitness.
#   3. vwsr. The decode cost ZERO vwsr (0.558371 both sides), so this should not move it either.
#      If vwsr drops materially, the inherited zeros are costing conversion and that is a trade to
#      look at, not a bug.
# Set it back to 0 to revert; 0 is the pre-19cm behaviour exactly.
ROUTING_SEED_ZEROS=1

# ── SEED-CHAIN SPEED (19ck) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ROUTING_FEAS_PAR=0 — run the feasibility projection's starts SERIALLY again. They run
# concurrently by default since 19ck: the starts are independent, and the 20:35 run spent 30.6 s
# on four of them. Read [feas-par] for the wall time.
#
# ═══ ARMED 2026-08-27. RAN ONCE. KEEP AT 0 FOR ONE MORE RUN, THEN REVERT. ════════════════════
# ── RESULT OF RUN 1 (21:06, 19cs serial) vs 20:17 (19cr concurrent) — same everything else ────
#     stage 1 band-aware      1.093 -> 0.7159         1.093 -> 0.7159      IDENTICAL breach
#     feas WINNING CHECKSUM   3127764860              3804879062           DIFFERENT VECTOR
#       Sigma / nnz           23870.000000000 / 254,205 on both            identical support
#     stage 2 exact LP        0.393 -> 0.2934 (22)    0.393 -> 0.3425 (10)
#     stage 3 targeted move   0.6965 -> 0.3405 (10)   0.7132 -> 0.6419 (8)
#     RECONCILIATION ERROR    1,243                   1,260
#
#   1. THE CONCURRENCY IS NOT THE RECON BREAK. Serial did not bring 1,243 back to ~1. Of the four
#      changes that landed together at 19ck this one is EXONERATED, two are other-brand config
#      edits with no measurable effect on TotalAV (see the list below), and the gateway set that
#      arrived with the Master MID List edit is what remains to explain it.
#   2. BUT THE TWO PATHS DO NOT AGREE ON THE SEED. Same breach, different vector — so stage 1 has
#      several optima at 0.7159 and which one it lands on decides the chain: 0.3405 concurrent
#      against 0.6419 serial. The concurrent seed was nearly TWICE AS GOOD, by accident. The
#      "IDENTICAL either way by construction" claim this file carried is now falsified by
#      MEASUREMENT, not merely by the argument below.
#
#   WHY 0 FOR ONE MORE RUN. One serial sample cannot separate (a) serial and concurrent each
#   deterministic and simply DIFFERENT, from (b) `band_greedy_shares` non-deterministic and
#   NEITHER reproducible. A second serial run settles it with no code change: 3804879062 again
#   means (a) and the concurrency is the variable; a third value means (b) and the
#   non-determinism is inside the projector, which this switch cannot fix.
#   CHANGE NOTHING ELSE FOR THAT RUN — the last two days went on untangling two changes that
#   landed in one gap. Do not put a third there.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ── WHY IT WAS ARMED (kept: the reasoning still stands, and run 1 answered half of it) ────────
# The TotalAV reconciliation error broke at 19ck and has stayed broken:
#     08-25 20:52  19ci  recon     1        08-26 20:49  19cm  recon 1,393
#     08-26 19:44  19ck  recon 1,254        08-26 22:18  19co  recon 1,260
#                        ^ the break        08-27 20:32  19cr  recon 1,243
# (An earlier note called 2,084 the break. That was a `company=Total Cleaner` run — different
# scenario, window, pool target and constraint set. Seven consecutive 19ck runs were Total Cleaner
# and had no business in a TotalAV series. Compare like with like or do not compare.)
#
# FOUR THINGS CHANGED INSIDE THAT GAP. This block said TWO until 2026-08-27; that was written
# after diffing only the Master MID List, and the other two were found by checking mtimes later.
# The correction is here rather than quietly fixed, because "exactly two" is the kind of remembered
# fact this file exists to stop.
#
#   1. data/mappings/Master_MID_List.csv          2026-08-26 15:56
#      17 rows flipped IsActive, nothing deactivated, no other field touched — a labelling
#      correction. But the engine gates the search on that flag, so the INPUT moved: capable set
#      34 -> 38 gateways, dropped-inactive 404 -> 387, other-brand 63 -> 76 (17 = 4 + 13, exact),
#      injected rows 151,216 -> 165,755, USA-only ids 6 -> 8. The four that joined the TotalAV
#      search are all PaySafe. 19ci read a list stamped 2026-08-19 16:41; 19ck read 2026-08-26
#      16:56. Correct data is still changed input. THIS IS THE ONE THAT MOVED TotalAV.
#   2. config/inputs/gateway_volume_overrides.json  2026-08-26 11:50
#      Five adyen-*-tcl `target 0 / apply_to vamp` entries REMOVED, woodforest-usd-tcl ADDED.
#      All -tcl, i.e. Total Cleaner — other-brand on a TotalAV run. NO EVIDENCE it touched
#      TotalAV: the three counters that would show it are identical either side of the gap
#      (15 switched-off gateways, 11 switched-off vampMid(s), 15 caps active, on 19cc/19cd/19cg/
#      19ci and on 19ck/19cr alike). Not proof of no effect — proof that nothing the log
#      exposes moved.
#   3. config/inputs/routing_restrictions.json     2026-08-26 15:55
#      adyen-usd-tcl-na added to usa_only_gateways. Also -tcl. Same reading as 2.
#   4. THIS SWITCH — 19ck's concurrent feasibility starts. EXONERATED on 2026-08-27: the
#      serial run read 1,260 against the concurrent 1,243.
#
# 0 tests the second WITHOUT TOUCHING THE DATA. Recon stays ~1,243 -> the concurrency is
# exonerated and the gateway set is what remains to explain. Recon returns to ~1 -> it is this.
# ANSWERED ON RUN 1: 1,260. Exonerated.
#
# THE CLAIM THAT USED TO SIT HERE WAS WRONG, and that is part of why this is worth running. It
# said the result is "IDENTICAL either way by construction, not by luck", on the strength of a test
# that pinned the RNG draws and the index-ordered reduce against a DETERMINISTIC STUB. That test
# never established that `band_greedy_shares` is deterministic when four copies drive the live
# numba projector at once — and three runs on byte-identical inputs gave band-aware breach
# 0.7159 / 0.7157 / 0.7159. The draws ARE still taken in sequential order and handed to the workers
# as data, and the reduce IS still serial in index order with the same strict `<`; what is not
# established is everything downstream of that inside the projector. Until it is, treat this switch
# as POSSIBLY ANSWER-AFFECTING, which is what the header's count of two does not yet reflect.
#
# WHAT TO CHECK ON THIS RUN, in this order:
#   1. [feas-par] WINNING SEED CHECKSUM — THE ONLY OPEN ITEM. Run 1 printed 3804879062 where the
#      concurrent run printed 3127764860. Run 2 must reproduce 3804879062 or it is (b) above.
#   2. RECONCILIATION ERROR — ANSWERED: 1,260, so not this switch.
#   3. [vterms] STRUCTURAL vs ABSENT (19cs) — ANSWERED, and decisively: 106,914.3 of 106,914.3
#      missing share is STRUCTURAL, 0.0 ABSENT, and the guard reconciled EXACTLY against the
#      Sigma_pshare deviation on the same page. Largest carrier is `paysafe - total av` at
#      25,801 — one of the four gateways that entered with the MID List edit, and the largest
#      POSITIVE per-band drift on the page at +296. So the renormalise-to-1 is CORRECT
#      arithmetic and belongs in the IN-SEARCH projector; that build is the next one, AFTER
#      item 1 is closed.
ROUTING_FEAS_PAR=0
# ROUTING_FEAS_PAR_WORKERS=4   # cap the workers; default is one per start
#
# ROUTING_SEED_LP_STALL=K — stop the exact projector's successive-LP after K CONSECUTIVE rejected
# steps. DEFAULT 0 = OFF, and off is bit-identical to pre-19ck.
#
# WHY IT IS OFF. The 20:35 run logged "breach 0.3518 -> 0.2216 in 12 LP step(s)" and then ran eight
# more, all rejected, while the trust region halved 0.00742 -> 0.000116: about 24 s of the stage's
# 69.5 s. Tempting — but a rejected step is NOT waste. Halving the trust region is the mechanism:
# the same direction can be accepted at half the size, because the linearisation is only valid near
# the current point. Stopping early is therefore ANSWER-AFFECTING and can hand the GA a worse seed.
#
# HOW TO DECIDE K. Every run now prints [lp-stall] with `stall_min_safe` — the longest run of
# consecutive rejections that a LATER step went on to justify. K is free on a run iff
# K > stall_min_safe there. Collect it over SEVERAL UNARMED runs before arming anything; one run is
# one sample, and the trailing steps are the ones with the least evidence behind them.
#
# AND NOTE THAT AN ARMED RUN'S OWN NUMBER IS CENSORED. Once armed, the loop breaks at K
# rejections, so a justified run of K or longer can no longer be observed and stall_min_safe is
# capped at K-1 by construction. An armed run cannot validate its own K. [lp-stall] says this
# outright rather than leaving a reassuring 0 to be misread.
# ROUTING_SEED_LP_STALL=3

# ── REVERTS (each turns off one shipped optimisation; all are bit-identical either way) ───────
# ROUTING_SOFTMAX_FUSE=0     # 19bx fused softmax        -> the untouched numpy reference
# ROUTING_CHILD_FUSE=0       # 19bx fused child          -> crossover + _mutate_fast, separately
# ROUTING_DELIV_FUSE=0       # 19ca scatter-into-cap     -> scatter, copy, cap
# ROUTING_ELIG_FUSE=0        # 19bs fused eligibility    -> the 19bm numpy chain
# ROUTING_PROJ_CELLBLOCK=0   # 19bt cell-blocked kernel  -> the flat kernel
# ROUTING_PROJ_LANES=32      # 19ch lane cap             -> 32 (64 is the shipped default since
#                            # 19ch: +3.4% at 11/11, p=0.001, against a +-0.7% floor. At P=35 a
#                            # cap of 64 and one of 36 dispatch identically, so this is NOT more
#                            # parallelism: it is ONE parallel call over all 35 candidates instead
#                            # of 32 plus a ragged 3. Scratch is P lanes' worth (~1.26 GB at P=35)
#                            # rather than the cap's — set this to 32 if memory is tight.)
# ROUTING_ROW_PARALLEL=0     # 19bn threading of deliver + softmax
# ROUTING_MUT_FAST=0         # 19bp sparse mutation draws — NOTE this one CHANGES THE SEARCH back
#                            # to the pre-19bp random sample, and forces the child fusion off too.
